{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California security deposit limit and return rules (AB 12)","requirement":"A landlord may charge at most one month's rent as a security deposit; qualifying small landlords may charge up to two months. The deposit must be returned with an itemized statement within 21 days after the tenant vacates.","key_value":"1 month's rent; up to 2 months for small landlords","coverage_conditions":"All residential tenancies in California; landlords owning only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total may charge up to two months' rent.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"landlord owning only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["Starting July 1, 2024, landlords who own only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total can charge up to two months' rent for furnished and unfurnished units if ownership is held by a natural person, family trust, or limited liability company (LLC) where all members are natural persons"]},"exemptions":"Landlords owning only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total, where ownership is held by a natural person, family trust or limited liability company of natural persons.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-07-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"AB 12","quoted_span":"Starting July 1, 2024, many landlords may only charge one month's rent for unfurnished and furnished units","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance security deposit interest","requirement":"Landlords of units fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance must pay tenants interest on their security deposit at the end of each year, plus a prorated amount if the tenant moves out before the end of the year.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Tenancies in units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["For tenancies in units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance, landlords must pay tenants interest on their security deposit at the end of each year and a prorated amount if the tenant moves out before the end of the year."]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"For tenancies in units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance, landlords must pay tenants interest on their security deposit at the end of each year and a prorated amount if the tenant moves out before the end of the year.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
